      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105783",
      ":question/problem": "Given that the random variable $X\u223c\u03c7^{2}(6)$, calculate $P(X < 4)$. Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4}x^{2}e^{-x/2}dx \\approx 5.17318$\n\n*The probability density function $\u03c7^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$f(x) = {(1)/(2^{k/2}\u0393(\\frac{k}{2}))x^{k/2 - 1}e^{-x/2},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
